WEBVTT

00:00:16.269 --> 00:00:17.269
Tess?

00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:18.269
Yeah.

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:21.269
Looks like you've been taking spin classes and not in the gym.

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.269
What are you talking about, Lois?

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:24.269
Censorship.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:29.269
I write an article against the VRA, and you turn it into Venom for vigilantes.

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:33.960
I didn't approve this article.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.689
I didn't approve any of these articles.

00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:41.689
Well, if you didn't greenlight this garbage, who did?

00:00:41.689 --> 00:00:44.689
You know, I have better things to do than deal with your mess.

00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:56.219
Excuse me.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:57.219
Tess.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:00:59.219
Vinyl Luther.

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:03.460
Luther.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.459
I thought...

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:05.459
Yes.

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:11.019
Well, rumors of my death have been greatly exaggerated.

00:01:11.019 --> 00:02:13.659
What?

00:02:13.659 --> 00:02:18.659
You got a hug for your long-lost daddy?

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.659
No.

00:02:19.659 --> 00:02:26.280
Clark told me about this other earth.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.280
You're from there, aren't you?

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.280
It doesn't matter where I'm from, Lutessa.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.280
I am still your father.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.280
And as far as this trusting world believes, the same man who successfully faked his own death.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.280
his own death.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.280
Which also makes you the same man who abandoned me.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.280
Interesting.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.280
Because in my world, you're the one who turned you back on me.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.280
I'm sure I had my reasons.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.280
Oh, you did.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.280
I neglected you, Lutessa.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.280
But I won't make that mistake again.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.280
Clark opened the door between worlds,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.280
and that's given me a second chance to put things right between us.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.280
To be the father you always wanted.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:15.090
What exactly do you?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.090
want, Lennel?

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:24.090
To provide for my family, for you, and for your brother.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.090
I was a fool.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:31.849
I turned my back on you for someone who betrayed me.

00:03:31.849 --> 00:03:34.849
Well, Clark was never yours in this world.

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:36.849
And Lex is dead.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.849
That is a lie, Tess.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:44.960
You saved Lex.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.960
And now he's out there, alone, somewhere.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.960
Because you discus.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:49.960
discarded him.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:56.659
And you know the crippling scars that that can leave on a child.

00:03:56.659 --> 00:03:57.659
Lutessa.

00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:04.219
Where is he?

00:04:04.219 --> 00:04:09.229
Tell me, now.

00:04:09.229 --> 00:04:16.060
I don't know.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.060
But I'm going to find him before you do.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.060
The boy doesn't need you.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.060
He needs his father.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:48.360
I say being a wanted man is supposed to be a bad thing.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:56.660
Are you peeking at your...

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.660
I...

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.660
Just a peek.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.660
Just a really quick peek.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.660
The government may have framed me as a terrorist,

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:03.660
but it would truly be criminal.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.660
to keep you from checking up on the world, wouldn't it?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.660
And while you do that, I'm going to, uh,

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:09.660
take a walk.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.660
I'm going to stretch my legs out a little bit.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.660
Oliver, you're stretching yesterday,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.660
led to you stopping two muggings and a very public bank robbery.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.660
That's right.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.660
I wore the hoodie.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:22.660
And if you get cut, you're going to be wearing prison orange,

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.660
which is not the best color on you.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.660
Hey, I just got you back.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:36.160
