Hit me like a banner headline.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:13.259
Go gorilla.

00:20:13.259 --> 00:20:16.259
Okay. Bad banana jokes aside.

00:20:16.259 --> 00:20:19.259
Lois, do you really think that you and I passing out a bunch of pamphlets

00:20:19.259 --> 00:20:22.259
is going to actually defeat the VRA?

00:20:22.259 --> 00:20:25.259
Actually, I had a different idea.

00:20:25.259 --> 00:20:29.259
I just need you to hack into a couple of national news websites.

00:20:29.259 --> 00:20:33.849
How many?

00:20:33.849 --> 00:20:34.849
All of them?

00:20:34.849 --> 00:20:46.059
Oliver.

00:20:46.059 --> 00:20:48.059
You can forget about looking into those kryptonite bullets.

00:20:48.059 --> 00:20:50.059
I found the shooter's crows nest.

00:20:50.059 --> 00:20:51.059
You'd leave an autograph?

00:20:51.059 --> 00:20:55.339
More or less, something scratched into the roof.

00:20:55.339 --> 00:20:57.339
I waited for my mother to get to the podium.

00:20:57.339 --> 00:21:00.339
I've only seen this one other place on the wall in Alexander's cell.

00:21:00.339 --> 00:21:02.339
He's the shooter.

00:21:02.339 --> 00:21:03.339
Don't worry, Clark.

00:21:03.339 --> 00:21:05.339
We'll find this guy.

00:21:05.339 --> 00:21:26.789
Tells us.

00:21:26.789 --> 00:21:28.789
I forgot to change the locks.

00:21:28.789 --> 00:21:36.220
Lionel Luther.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:38.220
It's a journal.

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:45.579
My doppelganger's life makes for a very interesting read.

00:21:45.579 --> 00:21:46.579
Alexander.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.160
Yes, signore Luther.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.799
Grazie.

00:21:56.799 --> 00:21:58.799
I tell you what, boys, I wouldn't get used to the view.

00:21:58.799 --> 00:22:00.799
You forget I know where you're from.

00:22:00.799 --> 00:22:03.799
People find out you're not the real Lionel.

00:22:03.799 --> 00:22:05.799
Not real. Why would anyone think that?

00:22:05.799 --> 00:22:08.799
I've been quietly reclaiming my assets for months now.

00:22:08.799 --> 00:22:13.799
Your illicit activities made it easy for me to buy you out at a bargain.

00:22:13.799 --> 00:22:17.799
And the Luther Court board has welcomed me back with open arms.

00:22:17.799 --> 00:22:19.799
Well, you know, in this world you murdered my parents.

00:22:19.799 --> 00:22:20.799
In mine, too.

00:22:20.799 --> 00:22:22.799
And I had a very good reason.

00:22:22.799 --> 00:22:23.799
Hit me.

00:22:23.799 --> 00:22:25.559
Security's on the way.

00:22:25.559 --> 00:22:27.299
We'll add assault and battery.

00:22:27.299 --> 00:22:30.150
Come on.

00:22:30.150 --> 00:22:32.660
Pass.

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:34.160
So what was that this morning?

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.160
How was that, uh...

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.660
Is that your idea?

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:39.660
You showed Daddy that you got the killer instinct, too?

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:40.660
Is that what that was?

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:43.660
Are you making an accusation against my son?

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:45.660
No one will take your word.

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:47.660
You're a convicted felon.

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:51.160
You should have stayed out of the spotlight,

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:53.660
but you wanted celebrity.

00:22:53.660 --> 00:22:55.160
You made one fatal mistake.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:56.160
You trusted them.

00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:57.160
The people.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:59.660
They're vulgar, uneducated, and stupid,

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:02.160
and they don't even know when you're fighting for them.

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:05.160
Must be heart-wrenching.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:07.160
Well, you got it all figured out.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:10.160
I'll tell you what.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:13.160
I wouldn't underestimate the common man at tomorrow's vote.

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:15.160
When the VRA is repealed and my name is cleared.

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:28.160
No, you're wrong.

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:31.160
Tomorrow the people will turn on you again, believe me.

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:41.619
You missed the mark, Green Arrow.

00:23:41.619 --> 00:23:46.279
Now it's our turn.

00:23:46.279 --> 00:23:47.279
Again.

00:23:47.279 --> 00:23:56.819
Again.

00:23:56.819 --> 00:23:57.819
Tess?

00:23:57.819 --> 00:23:59.819
Clark, I have been calling you.

00:23:59.819 --> 00:24:00.819
I've been busy.

00:24:00.819 --> 00:24:01.819
I found out who the shooter was.

00:24:01.819 --> 00:24:02.819
Alexander.

00:24:02.819 --> 00:24:13.220
I need to scan traffic cameras, retrace the steps.

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:17.220
Clark, Alexander's not the only Luther that's crawling back into our lives.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:20.950
Lionel's here.

00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:24.599
Lionel?

00:24:24.599 --> 00:24:30.599
He followed you from his parallel world, and he knows about Alexander.

00:24:30.599 --> 00:24:32.599
Even worse, he's already found him.

00:24:32.599 --> 00:24:35.599
I just got back from Father Sunday, Luther Corp.

00:24:35.599 --> 00:24:36.599
Alexander's all grown up.

00:24:36.599 --> 00:24:38.599
Family's back in business.

00:24:38.599 --> 00:24:45.000
Lionel's rebuilding his empire with Lex by his side.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:48.000
Clark, you saw the world that Lionel built over there.

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:52.000
Use the mirror box and send them both away.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:56.849
I destroyed the mirror box.

00:24:56.849 --> 00:24:58.849
Maybe Jarrell has a way to send Lionel home.

00:24:58.849 --> 00:25:00.849
Must know, Dad's been a little frosty lately, right?

00:25:00.849 --> 00:25:02.849
Maybe we should figure out a different way to get that genie back in the bottle.

00:25:02.849 --> 00:25:04.849
Yeah, I agree with Oliver.

00:25:04.849 --> 00:25:06.849
Don't you have other ways to deal with them?

00:25:06.849 --> 00:25:09.849
No one does anything till I get back from the fortress.

00:25:09.849 --> 00:25:23.039
This is your home.

00:25:23.039 --> 00:25:27.039
This is your home, Alexander.

00:25:27.039 --> 00:25:30.319
You'll be safe here.

00:25:30.319 --> 00:25:36.319
You always remember, son, a Luther's home is his castle.

00:25:36.319 --> 00:25:42.690
But this really isn't your home, Lionel, is it?

00:25:42.690 --> 00:25:46.690
And we both know this boy is sick and need serious help.

00:25:46.690 --> 00:25:52.599
Alexander, would you leave us a minute, please?

00:25:52.599 --> 00:25:55.950
It's all right. It's all right.

00:25:55.950 --> 00:25:59.950
So, Senator Martha Kent.

00:25:59.950 --> 00:26:05.950
I assume Clark told you about his journey through the looking glass.

00:26:05.950 --> 00:26:08.950
And he just called me about yours.

00:26:08.950 --> 00:26:10.950
You don't belong here.

00:26:10.950 --> 00:26:13.950
That's strange coming from you.

00:26:13.950 --> 00:26:16.950
Where does your son belong? Certainly not here.

00:26:16.950 --> 00:26:19.950
Well, on the side of the mirror, Clark is a force for good.

00:26:19.950 --> 00:26:25.950
And if you try to hurt him, I will destroy you.

00:26:25.950 --> 00:26:28.950
I find you very attractive, Martha.

00:26:28.950 --> 00:26:39.710
I understand why I had such strong feelings for you.

00:26:41.710 --> 00:26:45.079
I love to give you presents.

00:26:45.079 --> 00:26:50.259
There was a wristwatch.

00:26:50.259 --> 00:26:53.569
You remember?

00:26:53.569 --> 00:26:55.569
Lyle and I had nothing to hide.

00:26:55.569 --> 00:27:00.569
Engraved to Martha with deep affection.

00:27:00.569 --> 00:27:15.559
Clark.

00:27:15.559 --> 00:27:24.029
You may have used him in your world to kill Lex,

00:27:24.029 --> 00:27:29.750
but you won't use him in this one.

00:27:29.750 --> 00:27:30.750
Alexander.

00:27:30.750 --> 00:27:32.750
Is that true?

00:27:32.750 --> 00:27:36.750
You abandoned me in this world and wanted me dead in the next?

00:27:36.750 --> 00:27:38.750
Oh my God.

00:27:38.750 --> 00:27:40.750
Son, what have you done?

00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:45.750
Son? Isn't it a little late for that?

00:27:45.750 --> 00:27:50.700
In two separate worlds, you picked your son.

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:54.039
And it wasn't me.

00:27:54.039 --> 00:27:58.319
You loved her son.

00:27:58.319 --> 00:28:01.980
I was wrong, Alexander.

00:28:01.980 --> 00:28:03.980
I...

00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:08.680
That's why I came back here to find you!

00:28:08.680 --> 00:28:10.680
No second chances, Lionel.

00:28:10.680 --> 00:28:14.680
It's time to end this family feud.

00:28:14.680 --> 00:28:16.680
Alexander, please.

00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:17.680
Listen to me.

00:28:17.680 --> 00:28:18.680
I know I'm dying.

00:28:18.680 --> 00:28:21.990
I'm aging faster and faster.

00:28:21.990 --> 00:28:27.710
I have all of Lex's memories.

00:28:27.710 --> 00:28:31.710
And he despised every single one of you.

00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:33.710
Listen to me, son.

00:28:33.710 --> 00:28:35.710
Don't let hate master you.

00:28:35.710 --> 00:28:36.710
Make it your servant.

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:37.710
Use it.

00:28:37.710 --> 00:28:38.710
Let it build inside you.

00:28:38.710 --> 00:28:40.710
Your hate can make you strong.

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:41.710
I can teach you how.

00:28:41.710 --> 00:28:42.710
teach you how.

00:28:42.710 --> 00:28:45.710
There is nothing left for you to teach me.

00:28:45.710 --> 00:29:08.160
I'm taking pity on you, Martha.

00:29:08.160 --> 00:29:12.789
I know how much it would kill you to watch your son die.

00:29:12.789 --> 00:29:41.279
I was halfway to the fortress when I realized what you meant by taking care of the Luther's another way.

00:29:41.279 --> 00:29:43.279
You're looking for the Phantom Zone, Crystal, aren't you?

00:29:43.279 --> 00:29:45.279
You sent Slade there, didn't you?

00:29:45.279 --> 00:29:47.279
The VRA forced my hand.

00:29:47.279 --> 00:29:51.279
And when the justice system here is fixed, I'll bring him back to stand trial.

00:29:51.279 --> 00:29:54.279
How can you be so good, Clark?

00:29:54.279 --> 00:29:56.279
Because no one taught him to hate.

00:29:56.279 --> 00:29:59.619
Like Lionel taught me.

00:29:59.619 --> 00:30:04.589
Alexander.

00:30:04.589 --> 00:30:05.589
But don't worry.

00:30:05.589 --> 00:30:07.589
I took care of my father.

00:30:07.589 --> 00:30:10.589
And your mom too, Clark.

00:30:10.589 --> 00:30:12.589
What did you do?

00:30:12.589 --> 00:30:14.589
Clark.

00:30:14.589 --> 00:30:19.569
Part of growing up is letting go of your parents, Clark.

00:30:19.569 --> 00:30:22.569
Something you've always struggled with.

00:30:22.569 --> 00:30:24.569
Where are they?

00:30:24.569 --> 00:30:26.569
Back at the mansion.

00:30:26.569 --> 00:30:29.569
Or what's left of it?

00:30:29.569 --> 00:30:31.569
Since it's burning to the ground as we speak.

00:30:31.569 --> 00:30:32.569
You're not a killer, not yet.

00:30:32.569 --> 00:30:33.569
Not yet.

00:30:33.569 --> 00:30:34.569
You can come back.

00:30:34.569 --> 00:30:36.569
I'm the last Lex Luthor.

00:30:36.569 --> 00:30:39.569
After I die, there's no coming back.

00:30:39.569 --> 00:30:41.569
Alexander.

00:30:41.569 --> 00:30:43.569
No! Tess!

00:30:43.569 --> 00:30:45.569
I am done with all of you.

00:30:45.569 --> 00:30:50.230
And you?

00:30:50.230 --> 00:30:54.230
Always making yourself look better by making me look like some kind of monster!

00:30:54.230 --> 00:30:55.230
You're not him.

00:30:55.230 --> 00:30:59.230
You keep blaming everybody else, but look who has the gun in their hand.

00:30:59.230 --> 00:31:02.509
I know how you feel.

00:31:02.509 --> 00:31:07.329
After living in the darkness for so long,

00:31:07.329 --> 00:31:08.329
you feel.

00:31:08.329 --> 00:31:13.329
like you can't step into the light because it makes you feel ashamed.

00:31:13.329 --> 00:31:20.569
But Clark was the one that changed everything for me.

00:31:20.569 --> 00:31:29.519
He can do the same thing for you.

00:31:29.519 --> 00:31:32.519
Why would you want to help me?

00:31:32.519 --> 00:31:34.519
I'm your enemy.

00:31:34.519 --> 00:31:36.519
We've been locked in battle for years.

00:31:36.519 --> 00:31:38.519
You're not locked into anything.

00:31:38.519 --> 00:31:41.519
You had something Lex never had, and that's Tess.

00:31:41.519 --> 00:31:43.519
She loved you.

00:31:43.519 --> 00:31:46.519
I still love. I do.

00:31:46.519 --> 00:31:47.519
And I know.

00:31:47.519 --> 00:31:52.789
I know that I'm not perfect, but I'll always be there for you.

00:31:52.789 --> 00:33:43.269
You had a big win tonight.

00:33:43.269 --> 00:33:45.269
I think we'll still lose today.

00:33:45.269 --> 00:33:47.269
And after this vote, I'll be an outlaw forever.

00:33:47.269 --> 00:33:52.029
Hey, you might want to take a look at this.

00:33:52.029 --> 00:34:03.569
A beacon of hope shining light on the truth?

00:34:03.569 --> 00:34:10.050
It's our answer to the VRA.

00:34:10.050 --> 00:34:14.050
I like to consider myself a long-time supporter of these vigilantes,

00:34:14.050 --> 00:34:16.050
as they like to call it now.

00:34:16.050 --> 00:34:18.050
All of my hopes were confirmed.

00:34:18.050 --> 00:34:20.050
When I saw that mysterious letter S showing up everywhere,

00:34:20.050 --> 00:34:22.050
I knew it was you guys.

00:34:22.050 --> 00:34:23.030
And so what it was what it was

00:34:23.050 --> 00:34:28.050
Worth, Blur, thank you. You've already changed my life. Keep fighting. No matter what.

00:34:28.050 --> 00:34:32.050
I remember what it was like here in Metropolis before he came.

00:34:32.050 --> 00:34:36.050
You couldn't even walk the streets. But since the Blur came, we have hope.

00:34:36.050 --> 00:34:42.050
So I just want to let the Blur know that there are still people who supported, not one of them.

00:34:42.050 --> 00:34:49.050
Being a hero isn't about being able to save every person from a mugging or pull someone from a burning building.

00:34:49.050 --> 00:34:52.050
But to give people hope for a brighter tomorrow.

00:34:52.050 --> 00:34:53.050
The Blur is a simple thing.

00:34:53.050 --> 00:34:57.050
for integrity and morality and selflessness.

00:34:57.050 --> 00:35:01.050
If you're listening to this, Blur, thank you for everything.

00:35:01.050 --> 00:35:03.050
I want to be a hero of my kids.

00:35:03.050 --> 00:35:07.050
I want to be a hero that helps give faith in themselves.

00:35:07.050 --> 00:35:09.050
They can accomplish greatness.

00:35:09.050 --> 00:35:14.050
Thank you for helping me believe that heroes can and do exist.

00:35:14.050 --> 00:35:16.050
Blur, I want to thank you.

00:35:16.050 --> 00:35:20.050
As long as you're doing what you're doing to keep the people of our hometown safe,

00:35:20.050 --> 00:35:22.050
us boys and girls here can keep on doing our children.

00:35:22.050 --> 00:35:24.050
on doing air drops.

00:35:24.050 --> 00:35:26.050
I look at the blur and his powers that he has.

00:35:26.050 --> 00:35:30.050
They're amazing to be sure of, but that's no one inspires me about him.

00:35:30.050 --> 00:35:32.050
It's his character.

00:35:32.050 --> 00:35:39.050
When I see the blur and others like them turn their differences into strengths,

00:35:39.050 --> 00:35:44.050
it gives me hope that one day I can do the same.

00:35:44.050 --> 00:35:47.050
He's always there for us, standing up for us, and doing what's right.

00:35:47.050 --> 00:35:50.050
That's who a hero is, somebody who stands up for others.

00:35:50.050 --> 00:35:51.050
Everybody has the favorite hero.

00:35:51.050 --> 00:35:54.050
favorite hero. Well, my favorite hero is the blur.

00:35:54.050 --> 00:35:58.050
Thanks for being somebody that I can count on to do what's right.

00:35:58.050 --> 00:36:01.050
We love you, Blair. We're always here for you.

00:36:01.050 --> 00:36:05.050
I can't believe they'd risk coming out to defend me.

00:36:05.050 --> 00:36:09.050
You have no idea how much you mean to people, Clark Kent.

00:36:09.050 --> 00:36:19.440
I don't think a couple hundred testimonials will be enough to change the vote.

00:36:19.440 --> 00:36:23.809
Try a couple hundred thousand.

00:36:23.809 --> 00:36:25.809
All of them willing to step forward for you.

00:36:25.809 --> 00:36:28.809
They just needed a place to be hurt.

00:36:28.809 --> 00:36:29.809
You're an American here.

00:36:29.809 --> 00:36:56.389
You're an American hero, Clark.

00:36:56.389 --> 00:36:58.389
This historic vote is, of course, the first of its kind,

00:36:58.389 --> 00:37:02.389
with an unprecedented number of people going to the polls.

00:37:02.389 --> 00:37:06.389
And I've just been told, with all 50 states reporting in,

00:37:06.389 --> 00:37:11.389
we can announce that the measure to repeal the Vigilante Registration Act

00:37:11.389 --> 00:37:16.750
has passed.

00:37:20.750 --> 00:37:21.750
Thank you.

00:37:21.750 --> 00:37:25.750
You should thank your mom and Perry.

00:37:25.750 --> 00:37:26.750
They were my inspiration.

00:37:26.750 --> 00:37:27.750
inspiration.

00:37:27.750 --> 00:37:36.530
I thought that people had given into the hate.

00:37:36.530 --> 00:37:38.530
I didn't realize how much hope there was out there.

00:37:38.530 --> 00:37:40.530
I wish I would have had more faith.

00:37:40.530 --> 00:37:42.530
I want to be the man that you made that suit for.

00:37:42.530 --> 00:37:45.530
Clark, you don't need a suit to be the world's hero.

00:37:45.530 --> 00:37:49.530
Well, when I saw those people willing to defend me, it was inspiring.

00:37:49.530 --> 00:37:57.480
It got me to thinking that in order for the blur to be a true beacon of hope,

00:37:57.480 --> 00:38:01.039
maybe people need to see my face too.

00:38:01.039 --> 00:38:05.250
I've been to the future.

00:38:05.250 --> 00:38:09.250
And I saw the hero that I will become save the city.

00:38:09.250 --> 00:38:12.400
But I also saw me.

00:38:12.400 --> 00:38:18.400
me. I mean, Clark Kent, disguised behind glasses and a bad haircut.

00:38:18.400 --> 00:38:21.400
Well, I'm sure you still look very handsome.

00:38:21.400 --> 00:38:25.400
Mom, I just don't know how I can treat Clark Kent as a disguise.

00:38:25.400 --> 00:38:30.800
And you and Dad raised me be who I am right now, the real Clark Kent.

00:38:30.800 --> 00:38:35.800
What's real is your strength and integrity and compassion.

00:38:35.800 --> 00:38:40.309
As long as you remain honest to those things,

00:38:40.309 --> 00:38:44.309
it doesn't matter what you wear or what name you go by.

00:38:44.309 --> 00:38:48.309
because you'll always be my son.

00:38:48.309 --> 00:38:52.650
So you're saying I should become that hero and step into the light.

00:38:52.650 --> 00:38:56.239
You are the light.

00:38:56.239 --> 00:39:06.369
Your dad would be so proud.

00:39:06.369 --> 00:40:36.400
I'm beginning to forget things.

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:42.690
Remember what you did yesterday?

00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:52.340
What if I forget everything?

00:40:52.340 --> 00:41:09.119
If I forget you, I'll promise you.

00:41:09.119 --> 00:41:14.630
I promise you that I will make everything okay.

